// @kama/postgres — the PostgreSQL client for kama. It speaks the v3 wire protocol directly, in kama, over
// std::net; there is no libpq and nothing to install. TLS comes from @kama/tls.
//
// The shape of the package, as it fills in:
//   postgres            Connection, Config, Query and the `pg"…"` tag, Row and `column::<T>`, PgError
//   postgres::types     the value types PostgreSQL has and kama's std does not (Numeric, Interval, Inet, …)
//   postgres::pool      a connection pool shared by isolates
//
// The rules every module holds:
//   - Nothing from the server is trusted: every length is bounded before it is used, every text field is
//     validated as UTF-8, and a malformed message is `PgError::Protocol`, never a panic.
//   - A data error is a `Result`; a contract violation (a column index out of range) panics, exactly
//     like an index out of range on a collection.
//   - Blocking I/O with deadlines. A connection belongs to one isolate at a time and moves between them.
